 "structural_change": "After failed r2 route(-98TT/-28FF) and r3 reset gate, r4 fixes reset landing(main reset-only wrapper), replicated selects, and scale stage. Coordinator rejected its >9kb flop-ring per quantiser. SRAM successor replaces BOTH1024b9edge lines with16slot SRAM rings(4x128x256 macros each); read7behind write avoids collisions, then macro-local full-cycle read capture before S9 (SS clk-to-Q455.3ps), macro input negedge lockup. Exact same AQlat13/II1 and schedule. New safe432x345.6geometry, all43.2lattice, >=20um channels, full-face pins<=6/um; area priced in sizing.json before build. Main landing-fault face, registered KQ+2edge share and read-share variants are preserved; only issue module copied from paused r4. SRAM wrong-slot mutant isMUT7, main land-face MUT6 remains. Original SRAM gate now measuredTTsetup-6.329ps with clockspread194TT/169FF: new kit-local equal-actual-stage clock tree and independent nativeIO/allFF/eightmacro clock-graph audit; source/data/cadence unchanged.",
